WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.087
The federal mapping reuses the
controls Book 08 has already verified.

2
00:00:05.087 --> 00:00:10.276
It's illustrative, so validate it against
the system's own authorization boundary.

3
00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.850
Configuration and inventory first.

4
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:16.028
CM-2, the baseline:
the evidence is the Git

5
00:00:16.028 --> 00:00:19.688
commit and tag of the
rendered configuration.

6
00:00:19.688 --> 00:00:24.563
CM-3, change control: pull
requests with required review.

7
00:00:24.563 --> 00:00:31.162
CM-6, configuration settings: the agency's
stated profile, plus drift reports.

8
00:00:31.162 --> 00:00:36.483
CM-7, least functionality: a dedicated
DNS host, one role per server,

9
00:00:36.483 --> 00:00:41.113
the version hidden, and
recursion and transfers limited.

10
00:00:41.113 --> 00:00:44.964
CM-8, inventory: a CMDB
record for each server

11
00:00:44.964 --> 00:00:49.350
and an IPAM entry for each
address, with an owner.

12
00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:53.315
And SI-2, flaw remediation:
a supported BIND branch,

13
00:00:53.315 --> 00:00:57.376
ISC's announcement list
and vulnerability matrix,

14
00:00:57.376 --> 00:01:03.720
and remediation inside the timelines of
Binding Operational Directive 26-04.
